{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The sanding discs fit a natural next step after my cutting-wheel purchase: smoothing the edges of metal pieces before assembly.",
    "The screws and brass rods fit my repeated drilling and fastening purchases, while gloves and cut-to-size foam could support the adhesive work and padding needs of my DIY assemblies."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Both PLA filaments and the UV printing resin require a printing setup I have not shown a need for; my tabletop epoxy serves a different purpose.",
    "The foam-gun cleaner and emergency switch assume specific equipment or projects that my adhesive, tool, and hardware purchases do not establish."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Shared words like resin and adhesive seem to carry too much weight when the products have different uses and equipment requirements.",
    "My interest in making and repairing things seems to extend too broadly into specialized printing supplies and electrical controls."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My repeated purchases of rivets, threaded inserts, bolts, screws, and drill bits point toward practical fastening and assembly needs.",
    "Useful follow-on supplies should connect to an actual task suggested by my purchases, such as finishing cut metal or handling epoxy, without assuming additional equipment."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my hands-on assembly work but stretch that interest into specialized activities my history does not support."
}"}
